{"name":"Amethyst","hex":"#9966cc","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Amethyst","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A female given name."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Amethyst"}],"entries":[{"title":"Amethyst","blocks":[{"text":"Amethyst is a violet variety of natural quartz. Ancient Greeks wore amethyst and carved drinking vessels from it in the belief that it would prevent intoxication. Amethyst, a semiprecious stone, is often used in jewelry. It occurs mostly in association with calcite, quartz, smoky quartz, hematite, pyrite, fluorite, goethite, agate, and chalcedony."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b5/Amatista_Laye_2.jpg/330px-Amatista_Laye_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Amethyst","wikidata":"Q79058"},{"title":"Amethyst (mixtape)","blocks":[{"text":"Amethyst is the fourth mixtape by American singer Tinashe. Released independently on March 16, 2015, as a free project for her fans, the mixtape follows her continued emphasis on independent creative control, including self-directed visual work in the period after her debut album Aquarius (2014). The seven-track project, recorded in her bedroom during her Christmas vacation, features production from Ryan Hemsworth, Iamsu, and DJ Dahi. Titled after Tinashe's birthstone, Amethyst presents a blend of alternative pop and contemporary R&B, incorporating sparse piano motifs, heavy bass, and darker textures alongside mid-tempo tracks."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/4/48/Tinashe_-_Amethyst_%28cover%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Amethyst_(mixtape)","wikidata":"Q19801733"},{"title":"Lavender (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Lavender is a light shade of purple or violet. It applies particularly to the color of the flower of the same name."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9b/Lavandula_fields.jpg/330px-Lavandula_fields.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lavender_(color)","wikidata":"Q2468392"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1f/Geode_Reference_-25.jpg/500px-Geode_Reference_-25.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1f/Geode_Reference_-25.jpg/1280px-Geode_Reference_-25.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1f/Geode_Reference_-25.jpg/500px-Geode_Reference_-25.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGeode_Reference_-25.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/07/Citrine_am%C3%A9thys%C3%A9e.jpg/500px-Citrine_am%C3%A9thys%C3%A9e.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/07/Citrine_am%C3%A9thys%C3%A9e.jpg/1280px-Citrine_am%C3%A9thys%C3%A9e.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/07/Citrine_am%C3%A9thys%C3%A9e.jpg/500px-Citrine_am%C3%A9thys%C3%A9e.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACitrine_am%C3%A9thys%C3%A9e.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bc/Quartz_gisements.jpg/500px-Quartz_gisements.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bc/Quartz_gisements.jpg/1280px-Quartz_gisements.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":